            <AtypicalElectricalLoads deIcingCables="false" exteriorLighting="false" hotTub="false" heatedGarage="true" portableAirConditioning="false" pool="false" mixedUse="false" totalUnits="0" energyStarUnits="0" evChargingStation="false" outdoorGasAppliances="false" commonSpace="false" elevator="false" fitnessRoom="false" snowmeltSystem="false" unheatedGarage="false" />
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="3" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="0" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During the walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the following house components:

-Patio door

-Doors

-Receptacles

-Basement

The addition of insulation on the receptacles will help to reduce air leakages. Concerning the patio door, doors, and basement, please follow the recommendations. 

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>The exterior walls insulation was R-19 at the moment of the audit. We recommend upgrading the insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-28. The best practice to obtain better results is to add insulation from outside, this technique will give you the possibility to seal the building by wrapping it again without obstacles.  The best time to apply this technique is when it?????????s time to change the house's exterior siding.</mainWalls>
                <ceilings />
                <ceilingsCathedral>At the moment of the visit the roof insulation was R-40 for the flat roof section and R-28 for the cathedral roof section. We recommend upgrading the insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60.

 </ceilingsCathedral>
                <foundation>The existing foundation walls insulation is R-19, as well as the header joist. We recommend upgrading the insulation by adding R-10. The same upgrade is recommended for the header joist. A lot of energy can be saved when the basement is well insulated and sealed. </foundation>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement for the existing exterior doors and the patio door, by Energy star certified product suited for the northern climate.</windows>
                <VentilationSystem>The natural ventilation airflow is not calculated is not enough to ensure good air quality. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified. </VentilationSystem>
                <HotWaterSystem>Another solution to save some energy is the installation of Drain Water Heat Recovery, to recycle the heat from the hot water after usage. This system will recover the heat from the drained water to pre-heat the water in your water heater. This device will help you to reduce the energy required to maintain the water temperature in your water tank.



</HotWaterSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>Have you already thought about having a heat pump. This type of heating system can use up to 3 times less energy than a typical baseboard and needs electricity to operate. However this kind of system can?????????t operate on temperature below -250C, it then will require a secondary system to maintain the heat. In this case, the furnace can ensure the heat and the ducting system can be used by the heat pump to supply heat in the entire building.</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
